  "body": "It seems that the original wording of `If this algorithm was invoked by another instance of the \"unload a document\" algorithm` would translate pretty well to `recursiveFlag`, the concept used in the related `prompt to unload` steps. \n\nI propose these changes for clarity and consistency with `prompt to unload`.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3632/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 18, 2018, 8:29 AM GMT (9865125)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3632/5b653a9...9865125/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 18, 2018, 8:29 AM GMT (9865125)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3632/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 18, 2018, 8:29 AM GMT (9865125)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3632/5b653a9...9865125/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 18, 2018, 8:29 AM GMT (9865125)\">diff</a> )",
